window.GUIDE = window.GUIDE || {};
window.GUIDE.playthrough = [{"id":"day-1","era":"Pre-Hardmode","title":"Day 1: Spawning In","body":["You start with a {{Copper Shortsword}} or {{Copper Broadsword}}, a {{Copper Pickaxe}}, a {{Copper Axe}}, and a torch/ammo starter kit (exact starting metal is randomized per world between Copper/Tin, and the tools between Copper/Tin pairs). Immediately punch out a small 1x2 shelter, or just dig into a hillside, so you survive the first night.","Chop {{Any Wood}} from trees to get Wood, craft a {{Work Bench}}, and build a proper starter house: 1 door, 1 light source, 1 chair, 1 table, walls and a roof, all inside a fully enclosed space at least 6x9 tiles. Any finished house that meets the requirements will let an NPC move in.","Explore the surface in both directions for the day. Grab any chests, pots and Life Crystals you find, and note where the {{Demon Altar}} / {{Crimson Altar}} biome, ocean, and the Underground Jungle roughly are so you know which direction is which later.","Talk to the {{Guide}} for crafting hints. He will always be present at world start."]},{"id":"early-mining","era":"Pre-Hardmode","title":"First Ores: Copper Through Gold","body":["Head underground. Your starting pickaxe mines every pre-Hardmode ore up through {{Gold Ore}}/{{Platinum Ore}} with no power requirement, there is no hard gate here, just dig.","Mine {{Copper Ore}}/{{Tin Ore}} first, smelt at a Furnace into {{Copper Bar}}/{{Tin Bar}}, and craft an {{Iron Anvil}}/{{Lead Anvil}} plus upgraded tools and a starter armor set. Keep upgrading through {{Iron Bar}}/{{Lead Bar}}, {{Silver Bar}}/{{Tungsten Bar}}, and {{Gold Bar}}/{{Platinum Bar}} as you find each ore, deeper ore pairs generally spawn further down.","A {{Gold Pickaxe}} (55% power) or {{Platinum Pickaxe}} (59% power) is the best tool you can make before your first boss. A {{Tungsten Pickaxe}} (50% power) is already enough to mine a fallen {{Meteorite}} if you stumble onto one early; {{Demonite Ore}}/{{Crimtane Ore}} needs 55% power (Gold/Platinum Pickaxe) to mine reliably underground (a surface chasm exposes some that any pickaxe can take).","While mining, grab Life Crystals with a Lesser Healing Potion in hand to raise max HP, and pick up any Heart Statues, Gold Chests (need a Golden Key) and accessories you find."]},{"id":"boss-king-slime","era":"Pre-Hardmode","title":"Optional: King Slime","body":["{{King Slime}} is the easiest boss in the game and entirely optional. He has a small chance to spawn from killing regular Slimes, or you can force him with a {{Slime Crown}} used on the surface.","Any Copper-through-Gold gear handles him. He splits into small slimes when hit and hops around a flat area, keep circling and hitting."]},{"id":"boss-eoc","era":"Pre-Hardmode","title":"Boss 1: Eye of Cthulhu","body":["Once you have 200+ max HP and at least 3 NPCs living in your world, {{Eye of Cthulhu}} can spawn naturally at midnight (16% chance), or use a {{Suspicious Looking Eye}} at night to summon him immediately, no altar or special station needed.","Build a long flat arena with a couple of platform rows above it. He circles at range, then charges repeatedly once below 50% HP, keep strafing and firing.","His death opens no new areas, but he is the standard first boss kill and confirms your gear/arena approach works before you go looking for the evil biome boss."]},{"id":"evil-biome","era":"Pre-Hardmode","title":"The Evil Biome Boss: Eater of Worlds or Brain of Cthulhu","body":["Every world generates with either a Corruption or a Crimson biome (never both, pre-Hardmode). Find yours and prepare a {{Worm Food}} (Corruption, summons {{Eater of Worlds}}) or {{Bloody Spine}} (Crimson, summons {{Brain of Cthulhu}}), both craftable at a {{Demon Altar}} or {{Crimson Altar}} respectively once you have the right evil-biome materials.","Eater of Worlds is a giant worm, fight it in a straight dug tunnel and focus piercing weapons like {{Vilethorn}} since it splits into more worms as segments die.","Brain of Cthulhu hides behind Creeper adds; kill the Creepers first, then chase down the exposed Brain with a piercing weapon in a cleared room.","Both drop the {{Demonite Bar}}/{{Crimtane Bar}} materials (in bulk, beyond what you find naturally) needed for Shadow/Crimson armor and Nightmare/Deathbringer Pickaxes, worth farming a few extra kills here."]},{"id":"boss-queen-bee","era":"Pre-Hardmode","title":"Optional: Queen Bee","body":["In the Underground Jungle, break a Larva (Bee Hive-looking object) to fight {{Queen Bee}}, or bring an {{Abeemination}} crafted from Hive materials and use it anywhere.","She's a strong optional detour: her drops (the {{Bee Gun}}, {{Beenade}}, {{Hive Pack}}) give the Summoner class its first real pre-Hardmode weapon, and the Honey biome underneath the Jungle is worth exploring afterward."]},{"id":"boss-skeletron","era":"Pre-Hardmode","title":"Boss 2: Skeletron (Unlocks the Dungeon)","body":["Find the Dungeon (a gray/blue/green brick structure with a locked entrance) and talk to the {{Old Man}} guarding it at night to fight {{Skeletron}}.","Focus the head, not the two spinning hands; the hands can't be permanently killed and the fight only ends when the skull dies. Keep moving so you don't get pinned between the arms.","Beating him permanently unlocks safe(r) access to the Dungeon, full of stronger enemies, biome keys, and hardmode-tier vanity/weapons, and turns the Old Man into the {{Clothier}} NPC."]},{"id":"boss-deerclops","era":"Pre-Hardmode","title":"Optional: Deerclops","body":["In a Snow biome at night, {{Deerclops}} has a small natural spawn chance once you have at least one NPC, or force him with a {{Deerclops Eyeball}}.","A crossover boss with straightforward ground-slam and boulder attacks; any Skeletron-tier gear handles him for some extra loot on the way to the Wall of Flesh."]},{"id":"underworld-prep","era":"Pre-Hardmode","title":"Gearing Up For the Underworld","body":["Craft {{Molten Pickaxe}} tier gear from {{Hellstone Bar}}s (Hellstone needs a {{Nightmare Pickaxe}}, 65% power minimum, to mine, and burns you without Obsidian Skin protection). {{Obsidian Skull}} or an Obsidian Skin Potion, plus {{Obsidian}} armor from the Underworld/lava-adjacent areas, make this much safer.","This Molten-tier gear (weapons, Molten armor) is the strongest you can reach before Hardmode, and its pickaxe (100% power) is specifically what lets you mine the very first hardmode ore tier the moment you cross over."]},{"id":"boss-wof","era":"Pre-Hardmode -> Hardmode","title":"Boss 3: Wall of Flesh (Enters Hardmode)","body":["Build a long horizontal bridge across the entire width of The Underworld. Throw a {{Guide Voodoo Doll}} into lava (the Guide must still be alive in the world elsewhere) to summon {{Wall of Flesh}}.","It spawns behind you and slowly advances; just run in one direction across your bridge the whole fight, firing backward. Never stop moving or it will catch up and you'll be crushed against the map edge.","Killing it flips the entire world into HARDMODE, permanently: every enemy gets tougher, Cobalt/Palladium-tier ore spreads across the map, The Hallow appears, and a second stripe of Corruption/Crimson appears too. There is no undoing this, make sure you're actually ready."]},{"id":"hardmode-ores","era":"Hardmode","title":"Hardmode Ores: Cobalt Through Titanium","body":["Your Molten-tier pickaxe (100% power) can already mine the new {{Cobalt Ore}}/{{Palladium Ore}} scattered through the Cavern layer. Smelt into {{Cobalt Bar}}/{{Palladium Bar}} and craft a {{Cobalt Pickaxe}} or {{Palladium Pickaxe}} (110% power).","That unlocks {{Mythril Ore}}/{{Orichalcum Ore}} (110% power) and its bars, then {{Adamantite Ore}}/{{Titanium Ore}} (150% power, mined with a Mythril/Orichalcum Pickaxe). Each tier is a full armor set and weapon upgrade, don't skip the gear checks.","Break Demon Altars/Crimson Altars with a Pwnhammer-tier hammer (dropped by Wall of Flesh) as you go, each one broken has a chance to spawn more hardmode ore types across the world."]},{"id":"boss-queen-slime","era":"Early Hardmode","title":"Optional: Queen Slime","body":["In The Hallow at night, use a {{Gelatin Crystal}} to summon {{Queen Slime}}. She's the easiest of the early-Hardmode bosses and a good gear check right after Wall of Flesh, before the mechanical bosses."]},{"id":"mechanical-bosses","era":"Hardmode","title":"Boss 4: The Mechanical Bosses (Any Order)","body":["Craft the three summons at night from Hardmode Bars: {{Mechanical Eye}} for {{The Twins}} ({{Retinazer}} and {{Spazmatism}}), {{Mechanical Worm}} for {{The Destroyer}}, {{Mechanical Skull}} for {{Skeletron Prime}}. Fight them in whatever order suits your class, The Destroyer is easiest for ranged, Skeletron Prime is hardest for melee.","Build a long flat arena with several platform rows since all three fly or snake through the air. Cobalt/Palladium-tier weapons and armor are the expected gear check.","Each drops its own Soul type (Sight/Might/Fright); collecting all three lets you craft Hallowed armor and unlocks the Ancient Manipulator, which is needed to build the Titanium Forge/Adamantite Forge follow-on stations."]},{"id":"chlorophyte","era":"Hardmode","title":"Chlorophyte and the Jungle Push","body":["{{Chlorophyte Ore}} only grows on Mud Blocks in the Underground Jungle once you're in Hardmode, and needs 200% pickaxe power to mine, more than even an {{Adamantite Pickaxe}} (180%) or {{Titanium Pickaxe}} (190%) has. Craft a {{Pickaxe Axe}} or {{Drax}} instead (18 Hallowed Bar + one each Soul of Fright/Might/Sight at a Mythril/Orichalcum Anvil, all droppable by the mechanical bosses), it hits exactly 200% and needs no Chlorophyte at all to make.","Chlorophyte regrows slowly, so mine it a little at a time rather than clearing a vein completely. {{Chlorophyte Bar}}s make some of the best pre-Plantera gear for every class and remain relevant well past it."]},{"id":"boss-plantera","era":"Hardmode","title":"Boss 5: Plantera (Unlocks the Jungle Temple)","body":["After all three mechanical bosses are dead, a glowing Plantera's Bulb spawns somewhere in the Underground Jungle. Break it to start the fight immediately, so gear up first.","Fight her inside the Jungle itself; leaving the biome enrages her and drastically increases her damage. Phase 2 (below 50% HP) speeds up and adds homing seed projectiles, keep circling so her tentacles can't corner you.","She drops the Temple Key, opening the Jungle Temple (guarded by traps, bring a Lihzahrd-safe way through) toward Golem, and Chlorophyte spreads more freely after this fight."]},{"id":"boss-golem","era":"Hardmode","title":"Boss 6: Golem","body":["Inside the Jungle Temple, place a {{Lihzahrd Power Cell}} (crafted from Plantera's Temple loot) into the {{Lihzahrd Altar}} to summon {{Golem}}.","Destroy the arms first if you're melee, they block hits; ranged/mage can just focus the body. Once the body is destroyed the head detaches and flies around shooting lasers, chase it down.","Drops Beetle Husks and unlocks the Cultists at the Dungeon entrance, the last step before Moon Lord."]},{"id":"endgame-optional","era":"Hardmode","title":"Optional Endgame Bosses: Duke Fishron and Empress of Light","body":["{{Duke Fishron}}: fish him up with a {{Truffle Worm}} as bait in the Ocean. Widely considered harder than Plantera/Golem, fight in an open Ocean or sky arena, he's extremely fast.","{{Empress of Light}}: break a Prismatic Lacewing in The Hallow during the day (after Plantera). Fighting her at night is a much harder, unforgiving version of the same fight, stick to daytime for a first attempt.","Neither is required to progress to Moon Lord, but both drop some of the best accessories and weapons in the game."]},{"id":"boss-cultist","era":"Endgame","title":"Boss 7: Lunatic Cultist (Spawns the Celestial Pillars)","body":["After Golem, four Cultist enemies appear at the Dungeon entrance. Kill all four to fight {{Lunatic Cultist}}.","He teleports and casts fireball rings, then later summons phantom spectres; watch his cast animation to find the gap in each ring and dodge through it.","His death spawns the four {{Celestial Pillars (Solar, Vortex, Nebula, Stardust)}} across the map, the final step before Moon Lord."]},{"id":"lunar-events","era":"Endgame","title":"The Celestial Pillars","body":["Each Pillar (Solar/melee enemies, Vortex/ranged enemies, Nebula/mage enemies, Stardust/summon enemies that split) is shielded until enough of its own enemy type dies nearby. Fight in the open, this is a sustained wave fight, not a single boss.","They drop Fragments (matching each Pillar's theme) and Luminite, used together for the four endgame armor sets (Solar Flare, Vortex, Nebula, Stardust) and their signature weapons. Clear all four Pillars to unlock the Celestial Sigil."]},{"id":"boss-moon-lord","era":"Endgame","title":"Final Boss: Moon Lord","body":["Craft a {{Celestial Sigil}} from Fragments and use it in an open arena stocked with buff stations (Bewitching Table, Sharpening Station), platforms, and healing setups.","Destroy the two hands first, they deal the most dangerous close-range damage, then focus the eye/head. His true-damage attacks (Phantasmal Death Ray) ignore defense entirely, dodging matters far more than your armor stat here.","Killing {{Moon Lord}} completes the vanilla main questline and drops {{Luminite}} for the best gear in the game, plus a cosmetic ending cutscene."]}];
